Two decks share a shell here, and they win together. One is a reanimator deck that puts a seven-drop into the graveyard on turn two and onto the battlefield on turn three. The other punishes the table for drawing cards — and once Forced Fruition is out, every spell an opponent casts makes them draw seven into a board full of punishers. Nicol Bolas himself bridges both: he strips their hands as a creature and reanimates from ANY graveyard once he flips.

# The commander
Nicol Bolas, the Ravager :: four mana, flies, and every opponent discards on arrival. That is already fine; the flip is the point.
Flipping costs {4}{U}{B}{R}, and the planeswalker side draws two on the plus, kills a creature or planeswalker for ten damage, reanimates ANY creature or planeswalker from ANY graveyard on the minus four, and exiles a player's whole library on the ultimate. Do not rush it — flip on a turn where the minus four takes something worth taking.
Nicol Bolas, Dragon-God :: has every loyalty ability of every other planeswalker on the board, including the other Bolas. Its ultimate ends the game for anyone without a legend.
Spark Double :: a nonlegendary copy of a Bolas planeswalker, with an extra loyalty counter.

# Getting the fatty into the graveyard
Entomb :: one mana, instant speed, any card in the deck straight into the yard.
Buried Alive :: three of them at once.
Intuition :: three cards, and even the "wrong" two land in the graveyard where you wanted them.
Faithless Looting :: two down, twice with flashback.
Frantic Search :: free, discards two, untaps three lands.
Ripples of Undeath :: mills three every turn and buys one back for a little life.
Fact or Fiction :: whichever pile they give you, the other half is fuel.

# Bringing it back
Reanimate :: one mana, any graveyard.
Animate Dead :: two, and it can steal from theirs.
Necromancy :: flash speed, so you can rebuild in response to a wrath or reanimate at their end step.
Persist :: two mana for any nonlegendary creature.
Grave Researcher :: surveils every upkeep and prepares a free Reanimate once you have three creatures down there.
Command the Dreadhorde :: EVERY creature and planeswalker in every graveyard, paid for in life. On turn eight it usually ends the game.
Living Death :: your graveyard is the deepest at the table by design.
Kaya's Ghostform :: one mana of insurance on a reanimated fatty, and it beats exile as well as destruction.

# The Primordials, and the Cat that abuses them
Sepulchral Primordial :: takes a creature from EACH opponent's graveyard. Even in a fair game that is three bodies.
Diluvian Primordial :: casts an instant or sorcery from each opponent's graveyard for free.
Displacer Kitten :: every noncreature spell you cast blinks a permanent you control. Point it at a Primordial and you re-loot the table's graveyards every single time you cast a removal spell or a cantrip. This is the deck's engine, not a cute trick.
Noxious Gearhulk :: destroys a creature and gains you its toughness, and it blinks with the Kitten too.
Massacre Wurm :: a one-sided wrath against small boards, and every creature they lose costs them two life.
Hullbreaker Horror :: uncounterable, flash, and every spell afterwards bounces a permanent or a whole spell off the stack.

# Punishing the draw
Forced Fruition :: every spell an opponent casts makes them draw seven. On its own that is generous; with the cards below it is lethal.
Orcish Bowmasters :: a damage and an Orc for every card they draw past the first each draw step. One Forced Fruition trigger is six or seven pings and an Army that grows every time.
Sheoldred, the Apocalypse :: two life per card they draw. A single seven-card refill costs them fourteen.
Chains of Mephistopheles :: their extra draws become discards or mill. Against a table that is already being forced to draw seven, it empties hands and then empties libraries.
Howling Mine :: turns the punishers on during everyone's draw step, and you have the payoffs while they do not.
Monument to Endurance :: every discard of yours becomes a card, a Treasure or three life from each opponent.
Glint-Horn Buccaneer :: a damage to each opponent per card you discard, and a mana sink that discards while attacking.
Containment Construct :: lets you play the cards you discarded, so the looting costs you nothing.

# Interaction
Mana Drain :: counter, then spend the mana reanimating.
Counterspell :: the clean version.
Force of Negation :: free on their turn.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: one mana for anything noncreature.
Deadly Rollick :: free with your commander out.
Deflecting Swat :: free, and it saves Bolas from a removal spell.
Damnation :: your best creatures live in the graveyard, so a wrath costs you far less than it costs them.
Cyclonic Rift :: overloaded, it is the clear for a lethal reanimated board.
Feed the Swarm :: the only clean enchantment answer in Grixis.
Chaos Warp :: the second one, and it handles planeswalkers.
Baleful Strix :: a card, a flier and a deathtouch blocker that trades with anything.
Spellseeker :: finds Entomb, Reanimate, Persist, Counterspell or Dark Ritual.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a graveyard enabler and a reanimation spell. Entomb plus Reanimate with two lands is a turn-two seven-drop, which is the fastest thing this deck does.
Nicol Bolas, the Ravager :: cast him as a creature early for the discard, and flip him later when the graveyards are full. Flipping on turn six into a minus-four that takes back the best creature anyone has lost is worth far more than flipping on turn four for value.
Displacer Kitten :: prioritise her once a Primordial is on the battlefield. She converts every cheap spell in your hand into another round of graveyard theft.
Forced Fruition :: only deploy it with a punisher already down. On an empty board it is the best card you could give your opponents.
